# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitattributes  -  keeps line endings consistent across operating systems
# THE PROBLEM
# Windows ends every line with two invisible characters (CRLF); Linux and macOS
# use one (LF). Without this file, a Windows machine commits CRLF, the Linux
# build server sees LF, and Git reports every single line of every file as
# changed - which makes diffs useless and can break shell scripts inside Docker.
#
# THE FIX
# "text=auto eol=lf" tells Git to store everything with LF inside the
# repository, regardless of which machine committed it. Our GitHub Actions
# runner and Docker image are both Linux, so this is what they expect.

* text=auto eol=lf
# Files that must keep LF or they will not run on Linux.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
# Binary files: never touch these. "Fixing" line endings inside a PNG or a
# pickled model would corrupt it.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.joblib    binary
*.parquet   binary
*.ico       binary
*.joblib filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# The compiled report is a 5.6 MB binary that changes wholesale on every edit,
# so it belongs in LFS rather than inflating the repository history.
*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
